# Paths sync-main.ps1 keeps off the target branch (main).
#
# gitignore syntax, but this is not a .gitignore and git never reads it on its
# own - the script passes it to `git ls-files --exclude-from`. These files are
# tracked here on purpose, so they are backed up; they just must not be
# published. Ordinary build artifacts belong in .gitignore instead, which both
# branches share.
#
# The list has to name itself, or the sync would copy it across too.

.claude/
CLAUDE.md
DEVELOPER.md
sync-main.ps1
.syncignore
